  "title": "A great disturbance",
  "section": "Movie Facts # 1 of 10",
  "description": "As George Lucas' original draft of the screenplay developed in May 1974, its cast of exotic characters evolved significantly. Luke Skywalker went from a 60-year-old general to a member of a family of dwarfs; the Corellian smuggler, Han Solo, was envisioned as a large, green-skinned monster with gills; and Lucas based Wookiee Chewbacca on his Alaskan malamute dog, who often acted as the director's \"co-pilot\" by sitting in the passenger seat of his car. Finally, realizing his screenplay draft was way too long for a single movie, Lucas elected to create a trilogy of epic adventures, using the script's first third as the basis of the 1977 film."
}
